Document.description_en:
The Thunder Bay Port Authority proposes to rehabilitate existing dock infrastructure at Keefer Terminal.&nbsp;&nbsp;The project is funded by Transport Canada under the the National Trade Corridors Fund (NTCF).&nbsp; &nbsp;The proposed project is split into 2 phases with different timing, as follows:&nbsp; &nbsp;

&bull; Phase 1 &ndash; Cargo Ramps No. 9 - 12:&nbsp; permanent infill and decommissioning.&nbsp; &nbsp;All work is at deck level only. There are no in-water works, no pile driving, and no disturbance to the lakebed associated with this component.&nbsp; Construction, pending required approvals, is planned for fall 2026.

&bull; Phase 2 &ndash; Cargo Ramps 1, 2, 3 &amp; 4:&nbsp; replacement of Cargo Ramps No. 1 and 2;&nbsp; structural strengthening of Cargo Ramps No. 3 and 4;&nbsp;underwater pile repairs, deck soffit repairs, and pavement replacement across Docks 1, 2 and 3, and replacement of bollards, fenders, and curbs.&nbsp; &nbsp;Construction, pending required approvals, is planned for 2027.

